  "evidence": [
    {
      "kind": "aerial",
      "note": "Single-storey perimeter roof around a higher rectangular centre. The north front projects toward the parking lot and a faceted terrace projects south. Rooftop units occupy the north strip. Central roof sample (264,1145). The perimeter roof at (253,1129) samples #767768 and the pale field-side deck at (259,1162) samples #cecbb6."
    },
    {
      "kind": "lidar",
      "note": "Regional 2 m grid, heights above local ground. Median 6.5 m, P90 8.18 m, maximum 13.37 m. Northern and side roofs measure 4–5 m, centre 7–8 m. A narrow peak over the southern roof coincides with the rear of the scoreboard."
    },
    {
      "kind": "kartaview",
      "note": "Distant view from the parking approach shows the arched north entrance and the reverse of the scoreboard above the roof; trees interrupt the western end.",
      "frame": "79749199",
      "walls": [
        0,
        19,
        20,
        21,
        22,
        23
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "note": "North approach photograph shows a rounded glazed portal with a wedge-shaped keystone, dark windows, square piers, a projecting cornice and a shaped parapet.",
      "url": "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d50ee7_d25963ae1c884c6487f0f746c5186021~mv2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "note": "Unobstructed split-faced masonry close-up. PIL mean normalized (0.14,0.37) sets the primary buff-grey block colour.",
      "url": "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d50ee7_5281beb690554833907b6bbe8e8b67c0~mv2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "note": "Field side includes tall glass-block slots above dark horizontal glazing.",
      "url": "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d50ee7_d1620533a85e4a559ab13b891a6b13bd~mv2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "note": "Western Athletics identifies the second-floor offices and the Alumni Lounge with full-height glazing toward the field.",
      "url": "https://westernmustangs.ca/sports/2010/6/9/Facilities_0609105641.aspx"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Field-facing terrace curves in plan. The elevated scoreboard frame is open steelwork. The northern entrance has carved masonry and a shaped parapet. Side openings and entrance width are estimated. Laser returns reach 7–8 m over the inner lounge and 4–5 m at the outer terrace. The single dark rectangle on the north bow is the membrane cap of the projecting entrance portal. The scoreboard has a separate rear open truss spanning the field-facing lounge.",
